# Claude — this repo's own project-scoped `.claude/` is machine-local; the
# user/global config lives in `home/dot_claude/`, symlinked into ~/.claude/ by
# chezmoi. (Repo-scoped only — global excludes live in `home/dot_config/git/ignore`,
# NOT a blanket `.claude/` that would hide it in every repo on the machine.)
#
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/` on purpose: git never descends into an
# excluded *directory*, so a `!` negation inside one is silently inert. Ignoring
# the contents instead is what lets the one exception below actually apply.
.claude/*
# The one tracked exception: this repo's project-scope permission allows are a
# property of the repo, not a machine-local preference. `settings.local.json`
# stays ignored (below) and `worktrees/` stays ignored by `.claude/*`.
!.claude/settings.json

# Machine-local override — NOT a pattern this setup uses (every divergence lives
# in the committed settings.json contract). Claude Code auto-writes one on
# "always allow"/project-trust flows, so this line stops it being COMMITTED; it
# never stopped it EXISTING, and one carrying `Bash(gh api *)` sat unreviewed
# because git was told to ignore it. `home/.chezmoiremove` closes that half —
# removed on every `chezmoi apply`.
home/dot_claude/settings.local.json
